          "section_anchor": "S3.2 Gesundheitspsychologie",
          "printed_page": 27,
          "physical_page": 27
        },
        "cited_text": "Klassifikation von Stressoren (physiologisch, sozial, ökono-\nmisch/ \nökologisch, beruflich)",
        "residual_flags": []
      },
      {
        "content": "Stress reactions are described as cognitive, emotional, behavioral and physiological.",
        "citation": {
          "document_id": "bildungsplan-sek2-psychology",
          "document_title": "Bildungsplan Studienstufe Psychologie",
          "source_pdf_sha256": "a94fc8e1e5fb027b4d005b80a296aa4e5eaa99efe59fefedfe69e5ee3956da80",
          "section_anchor": "S3.2 Gesundheitspsychologie",
          "printed_page": 27,
          "physical_page": 27
        },
        "cited_text": "Stressreaktionen (kognitiv, emotional, behavioral, physiolo-\ngisch)",
        "residual_flags": []
      },
      {
        "content": "Physiological stress theories are Cannon's fight-or-flight and Selye's general adaptation syndrome.",
        "citation": {
          "document_id": "bildungsplan-sek2-psychology",
          "document_title": "Bildungsplan Studienstufe Psychologie",
          "source_pdf_sha256": "a94fc8e1e5fb027b4d005b80a296aa4e5eaa99efe59fefedfe69e5ee3956da80",
          "section_anchor": "S3.2 Gesundheitspsychologie",
          "printed_page": 27,
          "physical_page": 27
        },
        "cited_text": "Fight-or-Flight von Cannon \n• Allgemeines Adaptationssyndrom von Selye",
        "residual_flags": []
      },
      {
        "content": "Psychological stress theories include Lazarus and Folkman's transactional stress model with coping strategies and Antonovsky's salutogenesis concept.",
        "citation": {
          "document_id": "bildungsplan-sek2-psychology",
          "document_title": "Bildungsplan Studienstufe Psychologie",
